WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.167
-Adam Sandler, welcome back.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.334
Thank you for coming on.
-I love you.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.501
So good to see you.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:05.501
-It is always great
to see you, pal.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.567
It's great to have you here.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:07.634
-You got my beard.

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:08.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.667
-I'm copying everything you ever
did with your career.

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.167
I want to be you, man.
Come on.

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.467
-Is it itchy?
Itchy?

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.267
-I'm over the itchy phase.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.868
The itchy phase was tough.
-Do you wash yours good?

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:19.901
-Yeah.
Do you wash it?

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.367
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, I shampoo it.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.167
-Don't you forget
to do that sometimes?

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.334
And then you go,
"Ah, I forgot to shampoo it."

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:26.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.234
-I'm getting a lot of gifts,
beard gifts.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.234
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Brushes and oils and things.

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:34.300
Are you doing that, too?
-Uh, I get -- yeah, yeah.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.601
But I hate that oil feel

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.834
'cause it feels like it gets
on your regular cheek.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:38.968
-Yeah.
-And then you feel like

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:40.968
you got greasy cheek.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:43.100
-You got greasy cheek.
-But did you grow that

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.634
for "Hustle"?
-I --

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:46.467
I grew it for many reasons.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.100
-You look good.
You look good in it, man.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.734
It looks fantastic.
-No, no.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:53.467
-You were telling me backstage
I gotta get serious with you.

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.601
-Why?
-You told me backstage

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:55.901
you had hip surgery.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.267
-I had hip surgery, everybody.
It was sad.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.634
[ Audience "Awws" ]
-Dude, I feel --

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.400
What happened?
What are you talking about?

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.767
-It was funny.
So, I was --

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:07.501
It was aching.
My groin was aching.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.000
And then they said
it was in my hip.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.834
I thought it was my groin,
but it was my hip.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.701
So, I get the surgery.
And you've got to replace --

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:16.167
You replace your hip
when your hip's bad.

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:22.367
So, I go to the doctor
in the morning, very nice.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:23.434
You get the surgery.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.434
And I'm sitting in the bed.

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:30.234
And the man anesthesiologist --
is that how you say it?

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:32.300
-Yeah.
-He says, "All right.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.634
We're gonna knock you out.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.000
We're gonna put you
on some drugs."

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.767
So they put me
on some light drugs.

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.234
And then he said,
"We're gonna amp it up,

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:43.234
but when we bring you
into the operating room,

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:45.100
what music would
you like to listen to?"

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.667
And I go, "What do I mean?
Why am I listening to music?"

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:50.133
And then he goes, "Well, we like
to keep it fun in there."

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:53.300
And I go -- and I was already
a little dazed

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:57.734
from the mild drugs.
And so I'm going, "Uh..."

00:01:57.734 --> 00:01:59.734
He goes, "Who do you like?"
I go, "I don't know.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:02.434
I don't know who I like."
And so, he goes,

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.801
"I listened to Dolly Parton
on the way here."

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.234
And I go, "Yeah? Yeah?"

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:07.367
He goes,
"Do you like Dolly Parton?"

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.467
I go, "I think everybody
likes Dolly Parton."

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.167
[ Laughter ]
And then he's like,

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.267
"Yeah, all right."
So, brings me in

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:16.901
the operating room
or whatever it is

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:19.667
and amps up the whatever.

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.234
-Yeah.
And you start falling asleep?

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:24.801
-I'm not -- with the groin,
they have to numb --

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.501
I mean, with the hip,
they have to numb the bottom

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.334
like if you're having a baby.
-Okay.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:30.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.534
-So, they're numbing that,
so he has to keep me awake,

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:36.467
on drugs but be awake,
but he's holding me up, right?

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:38.334
They're holding me forward,
and they're drugging me

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:39.934
through the back
or something like that.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:43.968
And the man's face is right next
to mine, the anesthesiologist.

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:46.434
And I'm hearing this music,
and it's thumping.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.200
And it's going
boof boof, doo doo --

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.934
It's, like, a rockin' tune.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:51.801
-And he's talking to me.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:54.133
And I'm so on drugs
that I'm going,

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:55.701
"Am I supposed to answer you?"

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:56.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.701
And I'm looking at his mouth,
it's moving.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.934
I'm going, "Oh, he's
definitely looking at me.

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.667
He's definitely
asking questions."

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:05.334
And then I start going,
"But maybe I already responded."

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:06.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:08.667
So, I'm just kind of
looking nuts.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:11.667
And then I just --
I got no words out.

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.801
And I was going,
"Man, this is -- this is heavy."

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.467
And then he's looking at me,
and he's, like,

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.133
giving me a head nod goodbye.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:19.567
And the only words that came out
of my mouth were,

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.734
"This isn't Dolly Parton."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:25.501
And I was out.
-"That's not Dolly Parton."

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:28.200
Everyone loves Dolly Parton.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.234
-Which, uh --
which hip got replaced?

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:34.968
-My left hip,
which would be a great movie.

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:37.634
But, uh --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.968
But my --
"Did you see 'My Left Hip'?"

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.200
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.367
Anyway, so my wife was nervous
about my --

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:47.400
when I went into surgery

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.400
that they were gonna operate
on the wrong hip.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.868
-That happens, yeah.
-That happens.

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.234
Sometimes they make a mistake.

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:56.634
So she wrote on my right hip,
"No."

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:57.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:03.701
So there was a big "No"
in big, thick magic marker.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.567
-That's nice of her, though.

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:09.968
-The sad part -- I wake up,
and the no is still there,

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:13.133
and there's an arrow
pointing to my penis.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:17.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.934
-That doctor's funny!
I like that.

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:20.467
-The doc-- yeah.
-The doctor's funny.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.400
I like that doctor.
-Yes.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.901
-Can I say, you're on the cover
of "AARP" magazine.

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:28.868
-Yeah.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.467
Congratula--
[ Laughs ]

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:35.701
-That, uh -- that came
with the hip surgery.

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:37.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:39.567
-You get a hip surgery, they...

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:42.267
-They just got -- they called me
up, they said, "We heard."

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:43.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:46.000
"It's time.
It's time, old man."

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.434
Jimmy, my kids are here.
-Sunny?

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:49.701
-Yeah, Sunny and Sadie.

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:52.033
Yeah, they're right over here.
-Where are they?

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.601
Oh, yeah.
Hi, guys!

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:55.801
-Hey.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:59.033
-Oh, my God.
-Yeah, yeah, they came.

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:01.267
They've never been here!
-They've never been?

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.901
-They love you.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.167
You guys kidding me?

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:06.234
I've known you
throughout the whole years.

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.767
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Look at you.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:10.000
Welcome.
Isn't it fun to see dad up here?

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.033
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:13.000
[ Laughter ]
-It is, yeah, okay, yeah.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.968
Did they see you
when you're on tour?

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:16.601
-They hear me curse, yes.

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:17.801
[ Laughter ]
-No, no, no.

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.501
When you do stand-up,
when you do stand-up.

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:22.501
-They have come to my shows.
I don't know if they --

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:24.901
You've come to --
Did you come --

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:26.767
-Once.
-Sometimes they come on stage

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:29.300
when I go do tours,
and they come and sing a tune.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.300
-Oh, really?
-They come out and sing.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.467
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:33.467
-What is the song
that you guys like to sing?

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:34.634
-Taylor Swift.
-Yeah.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.734
-Taylor Swift, yeah, yeah, yeah.
Of course, yeah.

00:05:36.734 --> 00:05:38.300
Swifties.
Yeah, we're all Swifties.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:41.300
-Yeah, yeah.
-Well, that's fun.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.834
I wanted to ask you
about this tour

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:45.234
because I follow you
on Instagram.

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:47.868
And I see you're not doing,
like, just theaters

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:49.734
or clubs or whatever.

00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:51.834
You're doing stadiums
and arenas.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:54.901
-A lot of times,
it's big places, yeah.

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:56.734
-That's unbelievable.
-It's very cool.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.701
-I've been -- I started up --

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:01.167
Like, I started
doing stand-up again like

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:04.634
four or five years ago,
and now I run around and do it

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:06.234
for a couple weeks at a time.

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:08.434
And, yeah, it's been fun.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.734
I did my hometown.
I played my hometown.

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:12.734
I grew up in Manchester,
New Hampshire.

00:06:12.734 --> 00:06:15.200
-That's right.
-And I played,

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.400
for the first time,
in my hometown.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.968
I gotta tell you,
I was so nervous.

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:21.100
When you play your hometown,
there's something about it.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.634
I just didn't want to let
my family down and stuff.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:26.667
So, I'm on the side.
I was just terrified, you know?

00:06:26.667 --> 00:06:28.000
-Is that right?
-I really was.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.200
-But you're Adam Sandler.
-I -- I -- I --

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:34.133
They were so nice to me!
And, like, everywhere I walked,

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:37.033
people backstage are going,
"Ah, welcome home, Adam,"

00:06:37.033 --> 00:06:39.100
and all this great stuff.
So I was like --

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.400
Every time they were nice to me,
I was like,

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.300
"Oh, please,
don't let these guys down."

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:45.767
-How'd you do?
-I ended up doing --

00:06:45.767 --> 00:06:47.567
It was just warm.
It was great.

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:49.868
They were so nice to me.
It took me like

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:53.167
10, 15 minutes to be able
to not be so nervous.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.534
You know that weird feeling
sometimes --

00:06:55.534 --> 00:06:57.434
Even when you come out
to do this show,

00:06:57.434 --> 00:06:59.567
Sometimes you're out of body,
and you're saying words,

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:01.067
and you don't know
what's happening.

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:03.901
But I had that for a little bit,
but then I started locking in

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:05.567
on the crowd,
and they were just great to me.

00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:09.200
And then, my mom was there,
and it was her 85th birthday.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.000
And, like, everyone sang
"Happy Birthday" to her.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.601
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:17.334
-Happy birthday, Mom!
-Yeah, grandma.

00:07:17.334 --> 00:07:18.667
-She's got to be proud.

00:07:18.667 --> 00:07:20.200
And she's got
some great grandkids.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.634
-Yes, yes, yes, yes.
[ Laughs ]

00:07:22.634 --> 00:07:23.901
-Can we talk about "Hustle"?

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:25.000
Your movie, "Hustle,"
by the way,

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.767
is streaming
on Netflix right now.

00:07:26.767 --> 00:07:28.634
You're getting -- okay, sure.
Give it up.

00:07:28.634 --> 00:07:30.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:32.934
-You're getting rave reviews.

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:35.567
There's even some awards buzz
for you.

00:07:35.567 --> 00:07:37.534
-That's weird.
-And earlier this week --

00:07:37.534 --> 00:07:39.767
-No, it's well-deserved.
-It's cool. Thank you.

00:07:39.767 --> 00:07:41.267
-Earlier this week,
you were honored with --

00:07:41.267 --> 00:07:43.000
you got
a Performer Tribute Award

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.734
at the Gotham Awards right here
in New York City.

00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:46.067
-Yes, yes.
-Congrats on that.

00:07:46.067 --> 00:07:48.734
-Thank you, buddy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.567
-You were here.
It was amazing.

00:07:50.567 --> 00:07:53.334
-I have to --
It's nice,

00:07:53.334 --> 00:07:54.801
people being nice to me,
and thank you.

00:07:54.801 --> 00:07:58.300
But I, like, have to wear
to these award get-togethers,

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.534
I gotta dress up.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:02.701
And I don't --
You know, I'm not goo--

00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:05.634
I just don't like it.
I don't -- but I --

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:07.968
And my wife dresses up,
and she looks great.

00:08:07.968 --> 00:08:11.634
And it's kind of -- you know,
I should look good for her.

00:08:11.634 --> 00:08:12.834
So, I --
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.834 --> 00:08:15.000
But every time I say,
like, I give myself --

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.701
"Hey, that thing's on Thursday.
I should get a suit,"

00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:20.667
and then I go,
"Oh, it's already Wednesday."

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:21.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:24.501
And I always end up
just wearing my --

00:08:24.501 --> 00:08:27.501
Sunny's bat mitzvah
was like six months ago,

00:08:27.501 --> 00:08:29.133
so I always wear
the bat mitzvah suit.

00:08:29.133 --> 00:08:30.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.634 --> 00:08:34.234
-That's the one suit you wear?
-That's the only thing I change.

00:08:34.234 --> 00:08:36.434
I don't even change the tie.

00:08:36.434 --> 00:08:37.834
The tie -- everything --
The socks.

00:08:37.834 --> 00:08:40.501
Sometimes I change my socks,
but no one sees that.

00:08:40.501 --> 00:08:42.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.067 --> 00:08:44.167
-I gotta say, it's well-deserved
that you're getting these things

00:08:44.167 --> 00:08:46.801
and the awards buzz
because, you know, I'm a fan,

00:08:46.801 --> 00:08:49.734
but this movie moved people.
-Ah, thank you, buddy.

00:08:49.734 --> 00:08:51.701
-It was awesome.
-Queen Latifah, baby.

00:08:51.701 --> 00:08:54.033
-That's my pal.
That's my buddy.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:56.434
-Yeah.
-She's fantastic in it.

00:08:56.434 --> 00:08:58.501
-Yes.
-Everyone's in it.

00:08:58.501 --> 00:09:01.234
But, also,
who's the basketball player?

00:09:01.234 --> 00:09:02.834
-Juancho Hernangomez.

00:09:02.834 --> 00:09:05.000
He's phenomenal in the movie.
-Phenomenal.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.067
And you two together.
And, like --

00:09:07.067 --> 00:09:10.300
-Oh, what a nice guy.
He's just the sweetest guy,

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:14.033
not an actor, doesn't care
about acting at all, but just --

00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:16.100
He plays for Toronto.
He's playing a lot now.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:18.534
He's playing great.
And he just did --

00:09:18.534 --> 00:09:19.767
It's just amazing
to be with a guy

00:09:19.767 --> 00:09:21.801
who doesn't care
that he's good at something.

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:24.267
He's a great actor.
Every time, after every take,

00:09:24.267 --> 00:09:25.868
I go, "How did you do that?
It was amazing."

00:09:25.868 --> 00:09:28.300
He'd be like, "Do what?"
[ Laughter ]

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.801
-But it's like, I would say,

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:31.767
it's like a "Rocky"
for basketball kind of.

00:09:31.767 --> 00:09:33.968
-Ah, yeah, that's good.
-I felt so good.

00:09:33.968 --> 00:09:35.667
-Yeah, yeah.
-Like, it's just moving.

00:09:35.667 --> 00:09:37.434
It's exactly what you want,
and you're like,

00:09:37.434 --> 00:09:38.834
"Keep working, keep going,
keep trying."

00:09:38.834 --> 00:09:40.300
-Yeah, right, right.
-It's also funny.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.100
But you're amazing in it.
-Thank you.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.667
-I want to show a clip.
Here's Adam Sandler in "Hustle."

00:09:45.667 --> 00:09:47.434
Take a look at this.
-Thank you, Jimmy.

00:09:47.434 --> 00:09:50.501
-Obsession's gonna beat talent
every time.

00:09:50.501 --> 00:09:54.200
You got all the talent in the
world, but are you obsessed?

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.534
Is it all you ever think about?

00:09:56.534 --> 00:09:59.901
Let's face it --
it's you against you out there.

00:09:59.901 --> 00:10:02.734
When you walk on that court,
you have to think,

00:10:02.734 --> 00:10:05.167
"I am the best guy out there."

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:08.167
I don't care
if LeBron's playing!

00:10:08.167 --> 00:10:11.734
So, let me ask you again --
do you love this game?

00:10:11.734 --> 00:10:14.033
♪♪

00:10:14.033 --> 00:10:15.367
-Yes.

00:10:15.367 --> 00:10:17.634
-Is there a newborn kitten
purring in here right now?

00:10:17.634 --> 00:10:19.868
I couldn't hear you.

00:10:19.868 --> 00:10:21.934
Do you want to be in the NBA?

00:10:21.934 --> 00:10:24.400
-Yes!

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:28.000
-Well, let's make that happen.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.234
Never back down.

00:10:31.234 --> 00:10:33.834
-Yeah!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:10:33.834 --> 00:10:35.467
-Whoa.
-That's how you do it!

00:10:35.467 --> 00:10:37.067
Adam Sandler, everybody!
-Thank you.

00:10:37.067 --> 00:10:38.267
Thank you, guys!

00:10:38.267 --> 00:10:40.801
-"Hustle" is streaming now
on Netflix!

00:10:40.801 --> 00:10:43.601
Catch Adam on his stand-up tour,
"Adam Sandler Live."

00:10:43.601 --> 00:10:45.234
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:10:45.234 --> 00:10:47.167
Stick around, everybody.
Yes!

00:10:47.167 --> 00:10:49.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:57.300
♪♪

